Description: IIS web server logs (W3C) - every request, HTTP.sys errors and the site list
Category: WebLogs
Author: ArtefactForge
Version: '1.0'
ExportFormat: csv
OutputName: IisLogs
# IIS W3C logs in each site's folder (W3SVC<n> for web sites, FTPSVC<n> for FTP) under
# inetpub\logs\LogFiles, Windows\System32\LogFiles (servers upgraded from IIS 6) and any log folder
# applicationHost.config names on the system drive; and HTTP.sys's HTTPERR logs, the requests it
# rejected before IIS saw them. Exchange's OWA, ECP, EWS and ActiveSync traffic is in the Default
# Web Site and Exchange Back End sites' logs. NCSA and IIS native format logs, zipped archives and
# lines that do not fit their #Fields line are named in the .err.log, not parsed.
#
# W3C times are UTC whatever the "local time rollover" setting, which changes only the file names.
# Each #Fields line sets the columns for the lines after it, so a log whose logged fields changed
# part way through (IIS writes a new block in the same file) is read correctly. Fields the module
# has no column for, such as custom ones, are kept in Extra as name=value. A logged X-Forwarded-For
# is kept in ForwardedFor, and the lake's timeline takes it as the client address.
#
# IisLogs_Flagged.csv holds requests matching web shell, Exchange exploit, injection and scanner
# patterns, and POSTs answered by a script in a folder that normally holds static files: a triage
# aid for where to start reading, not a detection verdict. IisLogs_Sites.csv lists each site's
# applications and physical paths, from applicationHost.config when it was collected; without it
# site names are left blank.
#
# Requires names the default log folder only, so a server that logs only to a custom folder or to
# Windows\System32\LogFiles is skipped for now.
Requires:
  - '%root%\inetpub\logs\LogFiles'
Platform: windows
Elevation: live              # the folders are admin-only on a live system; collections read fine
Priority: 45
IoWeight: heavy
Timeout: 14400
Processors:
  -
    Executable: builtin:WindowsIisLogs
    CommandLine: --root "%root%" --out "%destinationDirectory%"
    ExportFormat: csv
